---
---

<div class="eng-card">
  <div class="eng-card-header">
    <div class="eng-card-title">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
        <path d="M12 2v20"></path>
        <path d="M17 5H9.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 0 0 7h5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 0 7H6"></path>
      </svg>
      <span data-i18n="vt_title">Valve Timing Diagram (0° - 720° Cycle)</span>
    </div>
    <div class="chart-controls">
      <button class="btn btn-outline btn-sm vt-mode-btn active" data-mode="realistic" data-i18n="vt_mode_real">Realistic (Overlap)</button>
      <button class="btn btn-outline btn-sm vt-mode-btn" data-mode="ideal" data-i18n="vt_mode_ideal">Ideal Boundaries</button>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="chart-canvas-wrapper">
    <canvas id="vt-canvas" width="600" height="340" class="eng-canvas"></canvas>
  </div>

  <div class="chart-footer-note">
    <span class="note-bullet">●</span>
    <span class="note-text" data-i18n="vt_note">
      Green zone denotes Valve Overlap (IVO 12° BTDC to EVC 10° ATDC). Both valves remain briefly open simultaneously around TDC to scavenge exhaust gases and draw in fresh charge via inertia.
    </span>
  </div>
</div>

<style>
  .chart-controls {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.35rem;
  }

  .vt-mode-btn.active {
    background: var(--accent-cyan);
    color: #04101e;
    font-weight: 700;
    border-color: var(--accent-cyan);
  }

  .chart-canvas-wrapper {
    width: 100%;
    position: relative;
    background: #090d16;
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-color);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .eng-canvas {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    display: block;
  }

  .chart-footer-note {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    line-height: 1.4;
  }

  .note-bullet {
    color: var(--accent-green);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
  }
</style>

